{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqeolw11e46","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"retire a note node without a successor via note superseded with validTo only","summary":"The graph store has no hard delete event for note nodes. To RETIRE a note that has no replacement (an auto generated transient with zero knowledge value), append a note_superseded event with validTo set and supersededBy omitted. graph-store.js replays note_superseded setting node.validTo from ev.validTo independently of supersededBy, so the note becomes non current. A non current note (validTo not null) is excluded from default search_knowledge, the gated RAG candidate pool, judge buildQueue orphan and edge items, and the judge dup cluster pass, while the node and its edges survive as bitemporal history recoverable via history or as_of. Note nodes are NOT in the overlay LOCAL_FIELDS list, so they persist only through the graph store event log, never the overlay snapshot file; the running daemon keeps note_nodes in memory in state.overlay, so a store level mutation requires a daemon reload or restart to take effect in live search and judge. emitDiff only emits note_created for brand new keys and never re emits note_superseded, so appended retirement events are safe from being clobbered by a running daemon save.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T03:56:49.381Z","vec":[-0.08435594290494919,0.03172418847680092,-0.018836386501789093,0.009940464980900288,0.07051994651556015,0.0005074419896118343,-0.05320853739976883,-0.021783731877803802,0.05501565337181091,0.04712589457631111,0.0630631297826767,0.1026354506611824,-0.015784166753292084,-0.03793806955218315,0.023070078343153,0.02859058789908886,-0.0032237027771770954,-0.047307197004556656,-0.03164370730519295,-0.027692491188645363,-0.041925981640815735,-0.05127894878387451,-0.013863181695342064,-0.014682849869132042,0.00828989315778017,0.05128155276179314,-0.08236707746982574,-0.010945255868136883,0.05991441383957863,-0.0087851807